{"id": "unknown-2026-06-03-014", "date": "2026-06-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["satellite_constellation", "space_defense", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Live coverage: SpaceX to launch 24 Starlink satellites on Falcon 9 rocket from Vandenberg", "content": "The Starlink 17-47 mission will see SpaceX attempt its 200th landing on the drone ship called ‘Of Course I Still Love You.’ Liftoff from pad 4E at Vandenberg Space Force Base is scheduled for 8:37:40 a.m. PDT (11:37:40 a.m. EDT / 1537:40 UTC). <a class=\"mh-excerpt-more\" href=\"https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/06/03/live-coverage-spacex-to-launch-24-starlink-satellites-on-falcon-9-rocket-from-vandenberg-3/\" title=\"Live coverage: SpaceX to launch 24 Starlink satellites on Falcon 9 rocket from Vanden", "sources": [{"name": "spaceflight_now", "url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/06/03/live-coverage-spacex-to-launch-24-starlink-satellites-on-falcon-9-rocket-from-vandenberg-3/", "type": "rss"}]}
